"--- flip-the-sign · seed 1 · difficulty 1
prompt   Solve for x.
display  equation "x ÷ −2 > 3" unframed [inequality-multdiv x / -2 > 3]
answer   choice x<-6
input    choice
hint     A negative multiplier turns the symbol round as well.
choice   x<-6 = x < −6
choice   x<6 = x < 6
choice   x>6 = x > 6
choice   x>-6 = x > −6
step 1   Multiply both sides by −2.   [3 × −2 = −6]
step 2   It was a negative, so the symbol turns round.   [x < −6]
miss     did-not-flip = x>-6   Multiplying by a negative turns the symbol round.
miss     lost-the-sign = x<6   The symbol turned, but 3 × −2 is −6.
miss     kept-both = x>6   A negative changes two things here: the symbol and the sign.

