choice   open-left = Open circle at −5, shaded left
choice   open-right = Open circle at −5, shaded right
choice   closed-right = Closed circle at −5, shaded right
step 1   No line under the symbol, so the circle stays open.   [circle at −5]
step 2   Shade right, toward the larger numbers.   [x > −5]
miss     circle-strictness = closed-right   −5 is not a solution here, so its circle stays open.
miss     shaded-wrong-way = open-left   Shading runs toward the numbers that satisfy it, right of −5.

